
COMMENT ON TABLE dd_jobs IS 'CURRENT PRODUCTION DISPATCH AUTHORITY (2026-09-15). This is the live, authoritative record for assignment/scheduling/evidence -- every portal (owner, provider, customer) and the dispatch resolver (dd_route_work_order) reads and writes here. Do not build new dispatch/portal features against dd_work_orders until the migration below is deliberately executed.';

COMMENT ON TABLE dd_work_orders IS 'FORWARD-LOOKING FOS ARCHITECTURE, NOT YET PRODUCTION-AUTHORITATIVE (2026-09-15). Written to by the Stripe webhook and dd_create_fulfillment_from_request(), but nothing reads it back: dd_route_work_order (the live dispatch resolver) and every portal ignore primary_provider_id and FOS state here entirely. This table models a richer future operating model (multi-tier compensation, full lifecycle states) for when DANI has a real multi-provider network with varied pay structures. Decision (owner-approved 2026-09-15): keep dd_jobs authoritative for now; do not wire dispatch/portals to this table piecemeal. Migrate deliberately, as one project, once provider-network complexity actually requires it -- not before.';
